The compilation errors indicate that `COND_CODE`, `IS_VA_ARGS_PRESENT`, and `UTIL_HEAD` macros are implicitly declared as functions, suggesting that their definitions are not available to the compiler when `ztest_assert.h` is processed. Although `zephyr/sys/util_macro.h` is explicitly included in `ztest_assert.h` (and a comment even states it's for these macros), the compiler still reports the issue.

A common cause for such problems, even with an explicit include, can be subtle interactions with other headers or preprocessor directives. Moving the include for `zephyr/sys/util_macro.h` to an earlier position in the file can ensure that these fundamental utility macros are defined before any other Zephyr-specific headers that might inadvertently interfere or rely on them.

The patch moves the `#include <zephyr/sys/util_macro.h>` line to be the first Zephyr-specific include in `subsys/testsuite/ztest/include/zephyr/ztest_assert.h`.

